  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of protection to vulnerable internally displaced, returnee and host communities women and families in North and East Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtIn response to the escalating humanitarian crisis in Ukraine, the&#xA0;project aims to provide timely, relevant, age- and gender-sensitive&#xA0;child protection&#xA0;and GBV services and&#xA0;awareness raising. It is centered in Northern and Eastern Ukraine (vulnerable raions of the&#xA0;Chernihiv, Sumy, Kharkiv, Dnipro and Zaporizhzhia oblasts, identified as being in high need by the Protection cluster).&#xA0;ltbrgtThe relevance of the project lies in the pivotal role coordinated humanitarian protection system&#xA0;plays in crisis response. It aims to address multi-sectoral needs of families lacking offline protection services due to the hybrid format of work of the relevant state agencies in the target&#xA0;regions, and humanitarian challenges, especially topical for the Sumy and Dnipro regions.lt/pgtltpgtThe projects main objectives are to provide and support timely&#xA0;unhindered access to psychosocial support and coordinated protection services to vulnerable girls, boys and families to&#xA0;provide&#xA0;them with&#xA0;life-saving GBV prevention and mitigation information and skills training and to grant&#xA0;improved access to safe, confidential, timely, and quality coordinated GBV services, especially to women and girls.ltbrgtBy linking service provision with awareness raising and capacity building of the protection actors, including state ones,&#xA0;tailored to the specific local challenges of the regions, the project aims to empower child protection and GBV prevention and mitigation response. It is centered around the imperative of the protection mainstreaming and adheres to the strict zero tolerance to SEA and safeguarding violations.lt/pgtltpgtThe project plans to cover 9335 individuals, including women, men, girls and boys. They will include vulnerable populations as well as protection actors&#xA0;who will continue to provide services after the project&apos;s end, guaranting its sustainable impact.lt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
